# Plan §7b's computed initialization into an explicit reference place (the sibling of
# unit_local_init_graph_place_refused, whose `Box: b` is callable): `@: Box b` is a typed reference, and `b: mk` -- mk's
# call, callable-first -- binds it only after the admission of mk's result to Box (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-
# 20260929-16).  mk returns an Other of another shape (two size_t, no int in v's place), and w reads v through b: the
# admission refuses the Other by the field b's Consumer reads (the receiving-use contract), the method's implicit throw
# `implements`, uncaught, stops R0.  Without the read the Other would be received.
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box
Other:
    size_t: p 1U
    size_t: q 2U
end: Other
fn: mk () Other
    return: @Other
end: mk
fn: w () int
    @: Box b
    b: mk
    if: b\v = 0
        return: 7
    return: 1
end: w
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: w(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
